Article 5 (Reporting and Supervision)
(1) An educational foundation receiving subsidies shall submit the following reports to the Minister of Education within seven days from the date on which the relevant circumstance arises: <Amended on March 16, 1991; January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. Where a subsidized project is commenced: A report on commencement of the project;
2. A quarterly accounting report concerning subsidies;
3. Where a subsidized project is completed: A report on completion (results) of the project;
4. Where the name, representative, or other particulars of an educational foundation change: A report on such change;
5. A report on any other matter requested by the Minister of Education.
(2) Where deemed necessary, the Minister of Education may have public officials under the Minister's jurisdiction audit documents and account books of a subsidized educational foundation to ascertain the progress and accounting status of its subsidized project. <Amended on March 16, 1991; January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; March 23, 2013>
